  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w500.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-W 504.02 Medical Eligibility",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 504.02 Medical Eligibility. To be medically eligible for MEAD:\n\n(a) An individual who is currently a medicaid recipient shall:\n\n(1) Have been determined eligible for aid to the permanently and totally disabled (APTD) according to RSA 167:6, VI, or aid to the needy blind (ANB) according to RSA 167:6, IV, within the 12 months prior to application for MEAD; and\n\n(2) Not have been terminated from APTD or ANB due to medical improvement during the previous 12 months; or\n\n(b) An individual who is not currently an APTD or ANB recipient shall:\n\n(1) Be employed, or self-employed, for pay, pursuant to the provisions of He-W 641.03(b)-(c), on the date of application and during the time eligibility for MEAD is being determined;\n\n(2) Have a medical impairment that meets the Social Security Administration’s Listing of Impairments in accordance with 20 CFR 404, Subpart P, Appendix I; and\n\n(3) Have a medical impairment that has persisted or is expected to persist for a minimum of 48 consecutive months.\n\nSource. #7644, eff 2-8-02; ss by #8292, eff 2-24-05; ss by #10321, eff 4-25-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w500.html"
}
